WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.867
Template review should follow untrusted data into output contexts.

2
00:00:03.867 --> 00:00:16.402
Reviewers can ask which templates render user-controlled fields, which
helpers return markup, which filters affect escaping, and which pages
display logs, translated text, rich content, emails, reports, or admin
data.

3
00:00:16.402 --> 00:00:27.537
Searching for disabled escaping, unsafe filters, raw HTML insertion,
untrusted template strings, risky helpers, and unclear rich-content
handling can reveal the most important review targets.

4
00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:35.405
Tests should verify that known risky fields and reusable components
continue to escape, sanitize, or reject untrusted content correctly.

5
00:00:35.405 --> 00:00:42.406
Regression tests are valuable for stored content because a value saved
months ago can become unsafe when a template changes.

6
00:00:42.406 --> 00:00:49.607
Teams should test emails, error pages, admin pages, reports, and reusable
components, not only the main customer-facing page.

7
00:00:49.607 --> 00:00:52.274
Rendering safety belongs to every output path.

8
00:00:52.274 --> 00:00:56.274
Logging should support investigation without creating new exposure.

9
00:00:56.274 --> 00:01:02.608
Logs should avoid secrets, credentials, tokens, session values, and
unnecessary sensitive rendered content.

10
00:01:02.608 --> 00:01:09.742
Monitoring client-side errors and suspicious rendering failures can help
identify broken templates or unexpected content.

11
00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:16.543
At the same time, reports and logs may contain user-controlled fields, so
operational tools must render them safely too.

12
00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.677
Remediation should fix the underlying rendering path.

13
00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:35.479
That may mean restoring autoescaping, replacing raw insertion, narrowing
helper behavior, sanitizing rich content with a reviewed policy, re-
sanitizing stored content, reducing response fields, updating tests, or
reviewing related templates that share the same component.

14
00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:41.480
Template security requires continuous review as features, content types,
and frontend behavior evolve.
